# Names-only template. Uncomment and populate only the entries needed for this workflow.
# No defaults or credential values are provided. Optional unset variables retain code defaults.
# Names-only template. Uncomment and populate only the entries needed for this workflow.
# No defaults or credential values are provided. Optional unset variables retain code defaults.
# PRIMARY — AWS (ECS Fargate / Lambda container), RPC provider A, keeper address A
# Copy to primary.env (git-ignored). In AWS, inject RPC_URLS and ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL from
# Secrets Manager / SSM Parameter Store, not as plain task-definition env vars.

# KEEPER_INSTANCE=
# KEEPER_CONFIG=
# Comma-separated, first is preferred; the rest are fallbacks. Use a different provider than the secondary.
# RPC_URLS=

# SIGNER=
# Key spec ECC_SECG_P256K1. The task role needs kms:GetPublicKey and kms:Sign on this key.
# AWS_KMS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_REGION=
# AWS credentials: on ECS/Lambda they come from the task/execution role — do not set keys here.
# Locally, run `aws sso login --profile <profile>` and set:
# AWS_PROFILE=

# Slack- or Discord-compatible webhook; empty disables alerts (they are still logged).
# ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL=
# Serves /healthz in `run` mode; omit for `once` (scheduled) deployments.
# PORT=
# debug | info | warn | error
# LOG_LEVEL=
# Optional: limit to a subset of jobs, e.g. JOBS=W5,W6. Unset runs all enabled jobs.
# JOBS=
